00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:18.380
[Kelly] - Look at you!
- Wowzers. Yeah.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:19.700
- Finally out of P.E.

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:22.906
- See, and these are reasons why

00:07:22.906 --> 00:07:24.617
15 year olds shouldn't have albums.

00:07:24.617 --> 00:07:27.172
[Kelly] - Or, why they should.

00:07:27.172 --> 00:07:28.109
- Or maybe they should.

00:07:28.109 --> 00:07:29.116
- I even look back at my stuff

00:07:29.116 --> 00:07:30.664
and I'm like, I always say
I should make an album like

00:07:30.664 --> 00:07:32.609
better with age and like recut things.

00:07:32.609 --> 00:07:33.814
'cause you're just babies.

00:07:33.814 --> 00:07:34.647
- I love that.

00:07:34.647 --> 00:07:35.480
- And your voice isn't like grown.

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:37.072
You know, you don't
know what you're doing.

00:07:37.072 --> 00:07:39.096
- Yeah, no. I didn't
know what I was doing.

00:07:39.096 --> 00:07:39.929
- I definitely didn't.

00:07:39.929 --> 00:07:41.597
- I can say that. I
mean, it was really fun.

00:07:41.597 --> 00:07:42.597
It was just a strange thing that happened.

00:07:42.597 --> 00:07:44.297
I still can't believe that that happened.

00:07:44.297 --> 00:07:45.720
- A lot of actors sing though. Like a lot

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:46.620
of actors would come on the show.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.231
I didn't really know that
before doing this show.

00:07:48.231 --> 00:07:50.463
But a lot of people are like
in bands or were in bands.

00:07:50.463 --> 00:07:52.570
- Yeah, they work well together.

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:53.901
- "I don't do it anymore."
And I'm like, "Whatever."

00:07:53.901 --> 00:07:56.061
I think it's awesome to
be creative like that.

00:07:56.061 --> 00:07:57.711
- Totally.

00:07:57.711 --> 00:07:59.257
- You should sing with
me one time on the show.

00:07:59.257 --> 00:08:00.090
- Yes please!

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:00.923
- Well, okay!

00:08:00.923 --> 00:08:02.470
Well let's talk about
Lessons in Chemistry.

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:03.303
Speaking of that,

00:08:03.303 --> 00:08:04.792
my recent album was called 'Chemistry'

00:08:04.792 --> 00:08:07.672
and I was in a bookstore
buying for books for my kids.

00:08:07.672 --> 00:08:09.498
And I was on my way out and it
was like sitting right there

00:08:09.498 --> 00:08:10.331
and it said, 'Lessons in Chemistry.'

00:08:10.331 --> 00:08:12.306
This was like a while
back and I was like, well,

00:08:12.306 --> 00:08:13.468
this is a sign I should buy this book.

00:08:13.468 --> 00:08:14.754
So I started reading it

00:08:14.754 --> 00:08:17.094
and then now it's like a
show. So I'm so excited.

00:08:17.094 --> 00:08:17.927
- Yes. That's the show now.

00:08:17.927 --> 00:08:18.825
- Have you read the book before?

00:08:18.825 --> 00:08:21.289
- Yeah. I got the book about two years

00:08:21.289 --> 00:08:22.505
before it was released.

00:08:22.505 --> 00:08:24.549
So it's been like my
little secret for a while.

00:08:24.549 --> 00:08:26.241
And now it's been just amazing

00:08:26.241 --> 00:08:28.345
to see it out in the
world and doing so well.

00:08:28.345 --> 00:08:31.974
[Kelly] - Yeah. It's just such a cool idea

00:08:31.974 --> 00:08:33.405
and how back in the day, how women had

00:08:33.405 --> 00:08:35.493
to kind of pivot and navigate.

00:08:35.493 --> 00:08:38.885
- Yes. It deals with that quite a bit.

00:08:38.885 --> 00:08:40.333
- Relevance would be a good word.

00:08:40.333 --> 00:08:42.359
Are you a foodie like you are in the show?

00:08:42.359 --> 00:08:44.573
- Oh yes, definitely. I mean,
I spend most of my time,

00:08:44.573 --> 00:08:46.031
if I'm not on set, I'm cooking.

00:08:46.031 --> 00:08:48.369
That's just what I do. I'm very
comfortable in the kitchen.

00:08:48.369 --> 00:08:49.594
- I really wanna be your friend.

00:08:49.594 --> 00:08:50.427
'cause then I'll just eat it.

00:08:50.427 --> 00:08:51.376
- Yeah, you can.

00:08:51.376 --> 00:08:52.815
- Explain the show and
the book to everybody

00:08:52.815 --> 00:08:54.059
that doesn't know.

00:08:54.059 --> 00:08:55.174
- Sure, the book

00:08:55.174 --> 00:08:56.308
and the show is based

00:08:56.308 --> 00:08:58.612
around this character, Elizabeth Zott.

00:08:58.612 --> 00:09:02.374
And she is a chemist who is not able

00:09:02.374 --> 00:09:05.974
to do her passions because,
you know, sexism is a thing.

00:09:05.974 --> 00:09:08.034
And so she ends up needing

00:09:08.034 --> 00:09:10.518
to do a quick detour from
the thing that she loves

00:09:10.518 --> 00:09:14.506
and gets a job as a TV show
host for a cooking show.

00:09:14.506 --> 00:09:18.682
And she fuses her love of
science and chemistry with food

00:09:18.682 --> 00:09:20.770
and becomes this big sensation

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:22.498
because she talks to
housewives as if they are

00:09:22.498 --> 00:09:25.127
smart, capable individuals.

00:09:25.127 --> 00:09:28.492
And so it kind of just is
tracking her and her life.

00:09:28.492 --> 00:09:30.526
It's a really, really beautiful story.

00:09:30.526 --> 00:09:31.359
- Incredibly powerful.

00:09:31.359 --> 00:09:33.630
- It says a lot about
life, the journey of life,

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:36.196
how it's unexpected and hard

00:09:36.196 --> 00:09:37.861
and beautiful all at the same time.

00:09:37.861 --> 00:09:39.832
- I just like that it's unexpected

00:09:39.832 --> 00:09:42.054
I never would've thought
I would did on this job,

00:09:42.054 --> 00:09:43.189
but I love that it's unexpected

00:09:43.189 --> 00:09:44.332
and you still can kind of incorporate

00:09:44.332 --> 00:09:45.664
things that you love into it.

00:09:45.664 --> 00:09:46.497
And I think that people should be

00:09:46.497 --> 00:09:47.330
open-minded about that.

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:48.163
- Oh yes.

00:09:48.163 --> 00:09:49.732
- Because sometimes we
get stuck in our things

00:09:49.732 --> 00:09:51.001
and you seem like a person that,

00:09:51.001 --> 00:09:52.486
like once you finish an
acting job, you're like,

00:09:52.486 --> 00:09:53.566
"Maybe I should skydive."

00:09:53.566 --> 00:09:55.151
- Oh yeah, definitely.

00:09:55.151 --> 00:09:57.121
- It's just like, I don't know
if I'll ever do that again.

00:09:57.121 --> 00:09:57.954
- That's what I'm saying.

00:09:57.954 --> 00:09:58.787
You're like, "Wait, I've done this."

00:09:58.787 --> 00:10:01.098
So I like to keep changing it up too.

00:10:01.098 --> 00:10:02.449
- I think that's the thing is like,

00:10:02.449 --> 00:10:03.282
then I find...

00:10:03.282 --> 00:10:04.115
- Monotony kills me.

00:10:04.115 --> 00:10:05.257
- Yeah. I have to change it up.

00:10:05.257 --> 00:10:07.686
And then I always end up
finding a way back to acting.

00:10:07.686 --> 00:10:09.414
But like for right now,

00:10:09.414 --> 00:10:11.233
I've taken pretty much a

00:10:11.233 --> 00:10:12.066
year off and all I've done is dance.

00:10:12.066 --> 00:10:14.022
I've been doing like six
hours a day of dance.

00:10:14.022 --> 00:10:15.455
- What kind?

00:10:15.455 --> 00:10:17.507
- A lot of ballet. But other things too.

00:10:17.507 --> 00:10:18.469
I've been doing tap now.

00:10:18.469 --> 00:10:20.044
- Did you relate it all to the character?

00:10:20.044 --> 00:10:22.187
- Oh yes, very much so. Yes.

00:10:22.187 --> 00:10:23.020
[Kelly] -Definitely the food part.

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:25.570
- I mean, of course there's
always things that I'm like,

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:27.558
oh, I have to understand that better.

00:10:27.558 --> 00:10:28.527
Like, I just am not innately

00:10:28.527 --> 00:10:31.177
as smart in science and
chemistry as she is.

00:10:31.177 --> 00:10:32.320
I had to learn about that.

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:34.957
But in terms of like a
woman with a passion, trying

00:10:34.957 --> 00:10:37.098
to make her way through like, of course.

00:10:37.098 --> 00:10:39.052
And also the way that,
you know, we try our best

00:10:39.052 --> 00:10:41.375
to quantify life and set
ourselves up for success,

00:10:41.375 --> 00:10:42.913
but there's just things
that are unexpected,

00:10:42.913 --> 00:10:43.864
things that happen.

00:10:43.864 --> 00:10:46.000
And I've of course had times in my life

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.152
where I've been like, "I don't understand

00:10:47.152 --> 00:10:47.985
why this is happening."

00:10:47.985 --> 00:10:49.546
And then in time it reveals itself why.

00:10:49.546 --> 00:10:51.976
And that life somehow organizes itself

00:10:51.976 --> 00:10:53.830
in a really spectacular way.

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:56.386
- Yeah. Wow. You should write
a book. You're good at this.

00:10:56.386 --> 00:10:57.219
- Oh, maybe I'll do that next.

00:10:57.219 --> 00:10:58.942
- I was like, "You should write a book."

00:10:58.942 --> 00:11:00.613
You've never done that, right? Try that.

00:11:00.613 --> 00:11:02.920
You have a very great
way of putting things

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:04.026
that are very relatable.

00:11:04.026 --> 00:11:04.859
- Oh, thank you.

00:11:04.859 --> 00:11:05.692
- But elevated. It's nice.

00:11:05.692 --> 00:11:08.075
Okay, so were you good
in science at school?

00:11:08.075 --> 00:11:09.983
- I mean, yeah, I'm competitive

00:11:09.983 --> 00:11:11.279
so I wanna be good at everything,

00:11:11.279 --> 00:11:12.603
but I'm not like...

00:11:12.603 --> 00:11:14.843
- I'm competitive and
I'm not good in science.

00:11:14.843 --> 00:11:17.113
- I was always way more
interested in the arts.

00:11:17.113 --> 00:11:18.874
Like any class that was like,
"We're gonna do a project."

00:11:18.874 --> 00:11:20.566
I would like hone in on
that and they'd be like,

00:11:20.566 --> 00:11:22.384
"Okay, we just wanted
like a tiny little thing.

00:11:22.384 --> 00:11:23.285
You've made a diorama

00:11:23.285 --> 00:11:24.760
and you didn't do the rest of your work."

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:25.920
And like, what's going on?

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:28.198
It's just very clear
on what I wanted to do.

00:11:28.198 --> 00:11:29.945
- Yes. Are you ready for a game then?

00:11:29.945 --> 00:11:30.778
- Yeah, yeah!

00:11:30.778 --> 00:11:31.960
- Cool, because we're
both competitive. Okay.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:32.793
- Okay, let's do it.

00:11:32.793 --> 00:11:34.822
- All right. Lessons in
Chemistry is on Apple TV+,

00:11:34.822 --> 00:11:36.343
you've got to check it out everybody.

00:11:36.343 --> 00:11:38.124
And The Marvels is in theaters now,

00:11:38.124 --> 00:11:39.737
which is also equally incredible.

